+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+A client that POSTs `POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal` with an `Idempotency-Key` and then retries
+after a lost acknowledgement gets back the current status plus an `idempotency` proof
+(`recognizedRetry`, `originalDecisionSequence`) — but not the `signalId` the first reply carried.
+With no `signalId` on the retry reply, a caller cannot match the retried call to the original
+durable signal record without scanning the event log for the event at `originalDecisionSequence`.
+The value already exists durably: the recognised retry authenticates itself *against* the committed
+`signal_recorded` event, whose payload carries the exact `signalId` the first reply returned.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- On a **recognised idempotent retry** of `execution.signal` (same `Idempotency-Key`, same request
+  body, same actor), the `200` reply's `data` additionally carries `signalId` — the original
+  durable value read from the committed `signal_recorded` event the retry matches, so it is always
+  equal to the `data.signalId` the first (fresh) reply carried. The existing `idempotency` block
+  (`recognizedRetry`, `originalDecisionSequence`) is unchanged.
+- The change is additive wire surface on ONE path: the recognised-retry reply of `execution.signal`
+  only. Fresh signal replies are byte-for-byte unchanged.
+- **Unchanged refusal semantics:** a mismatched actor or a wrong-kind committed event under the
+  same key still produces a `409` `GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT` with no `idempotency` proof — and it
+  must also carry no `signalId` anywhere in the reply, so a non-recognised caller never receives
+  retry proof or another caller's signal identity.
+- No other mutation endpoint (`approve`, `pause`, `resume`, `cancel`, `start`, `sweep`,
+  `wake-lease`, `claim`, `clear`, `amend_budget`) gains a `signalId`: none of them mints one.
+- Regression assertions added to the existing HTTP tests in `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs`:
+  - the recognised-retry test asserts the retry reply carries the original `signalId`;
+  - the mismatched-actor and wrong-kind tests assert their replies carry no `signalId`.
+  The positive assertion must fail without the implementation change.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `execution-signal`: The Runtime HTTP API's contract for submitting a signal to an execution and
+  for the endpoint's idempotent-retry behaviour — which replies prove a recognised retry, which do
+  not, and what identity information a recognised retry must return so callers can correlate it
+  with the original submission.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- none: the openspec/specs inventory is empty; this change introduces the first capability spec -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- `apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs` — idempotent-mutation classification
+  (`KeyState::Complete`) and the recognised-retry reply construction
+  (`reply_with_current_status` / `annotate_recognized_retry`).
+- `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs` — regression assertions in the three existing
+  idempotent-signal tests (recognised retry, mismatched actor, wrong kind).
+- Wire: additive `data.signalId` on the recognised-retry success path of
+  `POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal` only; no schema, core-crate, or dependency changes.
+- No CLI behaviour change: the CLI mints a fresh key per invocation and never takes the
+  recognised-retry path through these changes.
